#: src/core/command_def.h:6
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Computes a new image combining the image in memory with the image "
"<b>filename</b>. At each pixel location, the new value is determined as the "
"max of value in current image and in <b>filename</b>. This command is mask-"
"aware and will obey the mask if and only if the <b>-mask</b> flag is provided"
msgstr ""
"Υπολογίζει μια νέα εικόνα που συνδυάζει την εικόνα στη μνήμη με το "
"<b>filename</b>. Σε κάθε θέση pixel, η νέα τιμή καθορίζεται ως το μέγιστο "
"της τιμής στην τρέχουσα εικόνα και στο <b>filename</b>"

#: src/core/command_def.h:7
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Stretches the image to show faint objects using an hyperbolic arcsin "
"transformation. The mandatory argument <b>stretch</b>, typically between 1 "
"and 1000, will give the strength of the stretch. The black point can be "
"offset by providing an optional <b>offset</b> argument in the normalized "
"pixel value of [0, 1]. Finally the option <b>-human</b> enables using human "
"eye luminous efficiency weights to compute the luminance used to compute the "
"stretch value for each pixel, instead of the simple mean of the channels "
"pixel values. This stretch method preserves lightness from the L*a*b* color "
"space. The clip mode can be set using the argument <b>-clipmode=</b>: values "
"<b>clip</b>, <b>rescale</b>, <b>rgbblend</b> or <b>globalrescale</b> are "
"accepted and the default is rgbblend. This command is mask-aware and will "
"obey the mask if and only if the <b>-mask</b> flag is provided"
msgstr ""
"Εφαρμόζει τη συνάρτηση μεταφοράς μέσων τόνων στην τρέχουσα φορτωμένη "
"εικόνα.\n"
"\n"
"Απαιτούνται τρεις παράμετροι, <b>low</b>, <b>midtones</b> και <b>high</b> "
"όπου η παράμετρος ισορροπίας μέσων τόνων ορίζει ένα μη γραμμικό τέντωμα "
"ιστόγραμματος στην περιοχή [0,1]"

#: src/core/command_def.h:8
msgid ""
"Application of the generalized hyperbolic stretch with a symmetry point SP "
"defined as k.sigma from the median of each channel (the provided "
"<b>shadowsclip</b> value is the k here and can be negative). By default, SP "
"and the stretch are computed per channel; SP can be computed as a mean of "
"image channels by passing <b>-linked</b>. The stretch amount <b>D</b> is "
"provided in the second mandatory argument.\n"
"Implicit values of 13 for <b>B</b>, making it very focused on the SP "
"brightness range, 0.7 for <b>HP</b>, 0 for <b>LP</b> are used but can be "
"changed with the options of the same names. The clip mode can be set using "
"the argument <b>-clipmode=</b>: values <b>clip</b>, <b>rescale</b>, "
"<b>rgbblend</b> or <b>globalrescale</b> are accepted and the default is "
"rgbblend. This command is mask-aware and will obey the mask if and only if "
"the <b>-mask</b> flag is provided"
msgstr ""

#: src/core/command_def.h:9
msgid ""
"Auto-stretches the currently loaded image, with different parameters for "
"each channel (unlinked) unless <b>-linked</b> is passed. Arguments are "
"optional, <b>shadowclip</b> is the shadows clipping point, measured in sigma "
"units from the main histogram peak (default is -2.8), <b>targetbg</b> is the "
"target background value, giving a final brightness to the image, range [0, "
"1], default is 0.25. The default values are those used in the Auto-stretch "
"rendering from the GUI.\n"
"\n"
"Do not use the unlinked version after color calibration, it will alter the "
"white balance. This command is mask-aware and will obey the mask if and only "
"if the <b>-mask</b> flag is provided"
msgstr ""

#: src/core/command_def.h:10
msgid ""
"Applies a midtone transfer function autostretch to the image mask, if one "
"exists"
msgstr ""

#: src/core/command_def.h:11
msgid ""
"Computes the 'à trous' (starlet) wavelet transform of the loaded image on "
"<b>nbr_layers</b> layers, applies optional per-scale denoising, then "
"reconstructs the image, all in one step (unlike the two-step WAVELET / "
"WRECONS pair). The transform is linear (<b>type</b>=1) or bspline (<b>type</"
"b>=2).\n"
"\n"
"Optional per-layer reconstruction coefficients <b>c1</b>, <b>c2</b>, ..., "
"weight each scale on reconstruction (1 is neutral, 0 removes that scale); "
"layers left unspecified keep their neutral weight of 1.\n"
"\n"
"Per-scale denoising is applied to the detail layers before reconstruction "
"when <b>-denoise</b> is given. The method is bivariate shrinkage (<b>-"
"bishrink</b>, default) or thresholding (<b>-threshold</b>, optionally <b>-"
"hard</b> instead of <b>-soft</b>). The global strength is set with <b>-"
"k=value</b> (3 is neutral); per-scale strength factors with <b>-f1=value</b> "
"to <b>-f6=value</b> (1 follows the noise model, higher denoises that scale "
"harder). By default the noise of each scale follows the propagation model "
"from a single global estimate; <b>-perband</b> measures the noise of each "
"scale independently. With <b>-anscombe</b> the decomposition and "
"reconstruction are done in the Anscombe variance-stabilising domain, which "
"makes denoising a better statistical fit for Poisson-dominated (deep-sky) "
"data"
msgstr ""

#: src/core/command_def.h:13
#, fuzzy
msgid "Returns the background level of the loaded image"
msgstr "Επιστρέφει το επίπεδο φόντου της εικόνας που έχει φορτωθεί στη μνήμη"

#: src/core/command_def.h:14
#, fuzzy
